 "intro": "Before using Pythagoras' Theorem you must know which side is the **hypotenuse**. The trick: find the right angle, then look straight across.",
 "takeaways": [
  "Mark the **right angle** first.",
  "The side **opposite** the right angle is the **hypotenuse**.",
  "The hypotenuse is always the **longest** side — however the triangle is turned.",
  "Pythagoras' Theorem can only be used in a **right-angled** triangle."
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Why \"opposite\"?",
   "text": "The two shorter sides **meet at** the right angle; the hypotenuse is the only side that does not touch it."
  }
 ],
 "challengeIntro": "Quick checks — pick the right answer."
